vllm-flash-attn: build against C++20, not C++17.

vllm-flash-attn hard-codes C++17 in two places: the project-wide
CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD in CMakeLists.txt, and a per-target CXX_STANDARD property
set inside define_gpu_extension_target() (cmake/utils.cmake) that overrides
the project default for every extension target (_vllm_fa2_C, _vllm_fa3_C,
...). CMake therefore emits -std=c++17 on the compile line regardless of the
project-wide setting.

vllm's own top-level CMakeLists.txt already builds against C++20
(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 20), and current ATen headers hard-require it:

  /usr/include/ATen/ATen.h:4:2: error: #error C++20 or later compatible
  compiler is required to use ATen.

sci-ml/pytorch-9999 has moved to a version whose ATen headers enforce this,
so any TU that includes torch/ATen headers while compiled at -std=c++17
(csrc/flash_attn/flash_api.cpp, via _vllm_fa2_C) now fails to compile. Bump
both sites to C++20 to match vllm and the installed torch.

Tested against vllm-project/flash-attention @ 2c839c3 (pin from vllm main).

--- CMakeLists.txt.orig
+++ CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.26)

 project(vllm_flash_attn LANGUAGES CXX CUDA)
-set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 17)
+set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 20)
 set(CMAKE_CXX_EXTENSIONS OFF)

 set(FA2_ENABLED ON)
--- cmake/utils.cmake.orig
+++ cmake/utils.cmake
@@ -443,7 +443,7 @@
     add_dependencies(${GPU_MOD_NAME} hipify${GPU_MOD_NAME})
   endif()

-  set_property(TARGET ${GPU_MOD_NAME} PROPERTY CXX_STANDARD 17)
+  set_property(TARGET ${GPU_MOD_NAME} PROPERTY CXX_STANDARD 20)

   target_compile_options(${GPU_MOD_NAME} PRIVATE
     $<$<COMPILE_LANGUAGE:${GPU_LANGUAGE}>:${GPU_COMPILE_FLAGS}>)
